... very much different than any hack i've encountered before! speaking
of sounds ... will there be more things to hear in nethack? the sounds
in nethack2.3 are mostly inert except for the ominous hissing of the
cockatrice. with the advent of more sounds is there a way to go deaf?
the zig-zag wand of lightning and the true fireball spell could be
accompanied by a thunderclap and kaboom, respectively, which would make
the player go deaf for n rounds. the true fireball spell seems to be
the easiest to implement: a normal blast of fire, except it doesn't
bounce and when it reaches the end of it's random extent it detonates
out over a random odd-integer square centered at the end-point of the
original ray. of course the blast is constrained by walls but could
ooze out into corridors. blast zones of 1x1, 3x3, 5x5, 7x7, 9x9, and
11x11 are probably a sufficient set. for the case of a 1x1 blast zone
the fireball spell would not appear to be any different than a normal
blast of fire. of course, if the extent of the original ray is too
small and the blast zone too large, you/your possessions undergo fire
damage. it strikes me that lightning could be implemented as a series
of n (lets say n = 3 to 5) successive lightning blasts of a random
extent (lets say l = 1 to 3) where each successive blast continues in
the same direction as the original blast (bouncing taken into account)
except that there is a chance that a successive blast could be displaced
1 space orthogonal to the direction of the blast. okay this requires
some more thought so maybe it should wait until nethack3.0 is released
and tried.

